WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.760
For over a century, standard medicine has operated on chemical reductionism.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.260
This means engineering a single synthetic compound to forcefully block a specific receptor

3
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.860
or shut down an enzyme.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.500
But biological networks do not accept this passively.

5
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.080
When you force one receptor, the human body pushes back.

6
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.480
It down regulates receptors, it builds tolerance, and it actively fights the intervention.

7
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.520
That biological pushback triggers a cascade of negative side effects throughout the body.

8
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.940
The devastating opioid crisis is the clearest consequence of trying to force a complex system

9
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.800
with a single synthetic target.

10
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.240
Cellular pathways operate as coordinated networks, not simple mechanical switches.

11
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.820
Aggressively forcing one component will inevitably cause compensatory harm in another.

12
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.480
We compound this error with how we administer these chemicals.

13
00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.920
Today, doctors prescribe a fixed, static dose based entirely on a single snapshot taken

14
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.520
during an isolated clinic visit.

15
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:08.740
This chart contrasts that static dosing model on the left against actual biological reality

16
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.340
on the right.

17
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.520
Human biology constantly moves in fluctuating circadian, endocrine, and inflammatory cycles.

18
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:21.440
Because internal signaling fluctuates continually, a rigid dose inevitably drifts out of alignment

19
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.980
with the patient's physiological state within weeks.

20
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.040
Looking at this text comparison, the core issue becomes obvious.

21
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.760
Standard medicine relies on doses set for a statistical average patient.

22
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.440
That average person does not actually exist.

23
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.420
To genuinely heal, we have to stop forcing synthetic chemicals at generalized dosages

24
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.580
and pivot toward therapies that actively read and instruct the body's natural rhythms.

25
00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.360
The human physiology already knows how to repair itself.

26
00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:58.200
Founder Boris Markosian realized that cellular repair is naturally orchestrated by multi-protein

27
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.780
signaling ensembles that constantly maintain the body's balance.

28
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.660
In biology, form dictates function.

29
00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.780
A signaling protein must maintain its precise three-dimensional folded shape to physically

30
00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.520
connect with a cell surface receptor and initiate cellular repair.

31
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.060
But there is a massive roadblock.

32
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.680
Standard biomanufacturing relies on extreme heat and harsh chemicals to extract and sterilize

33
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.640
biological tissues.

34
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.280
As the temperature rises, these delicate three-dimensional structures physically melt and unravel.

35
00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.860
Once that heat deforms the protein, it loses its structural integrity.

36
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.680
It physically cannot slot into its target receptor, and its instructions are permanently destroyed.

37
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:46.860
This thermal destruction is the specific reason standard pharmacology has failed to successfully

38
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.040
harness the body's endogenous healing proteins on a wide scale.

39
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.600
The true barrier to advanced biologics is a thermodynamic engineering failure in our

40
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.580
tissue processing, not a lack of scientific discovery.

41
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:06.040
Markosian engineered a direct solution to this thermal barrier, the high-fidelity bioprocessing protocol.

42
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.200
Instead of relying on heat, the protocol extends the duration of the enzymatic digestion process.

43
00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.940
By giving the enzymes more time, the system can strictly cap the core temperature well

44
00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.940
below the point where proteins begin to unravel.

45
00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:24.300
The process ends with a thermodynamic cold stop.

46
00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.020
The system rapidly drops both the pH level and the temperature, halting the chemical

47
00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.160
extraction instantly without depositing any damaging heat into the proteins.

48
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:41.960
This low-heat protocol yields a distinct biological composition called the thermosensitive peptidome.

49
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:49.180
It is a completely intact, multi-protein ensemble, isolated between 3 and 100 kilodaltons.

50
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:54.140
Because it never touches high heat, this ensemble retains perfectly folded,

51
00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.420
sequence-verified signaling proteins like EGF, HGF, and FGF2.

52
00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:04.920
Their precise shapes and their ability to bind to cellular receptors remain fully intact.

53
00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:11.680
By solving the heat problem, we can successfully bottle the exact physiological instructions the

54
00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.360
body uses to heal and deliver them in their fully active state.

55
00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.780
Delivering a dynamic, living biological therapy requires a tracking system that can monitor the

56
00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.240
body's continuous physiological changes. Instead of relying on isolated clinic visits,

57
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.740
patients use a wearable digital ring and a sensor patch to continuously track their body's

58
00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:38.000
stress signals day by day. This continuous data feeds into a specialized AI mapping tool,

59
00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.580
mapping the body's complex biological network in a hyperbolic space to trace individual signals.

60
00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.740
The system uses strict receptor-level evidence to calculate exactly how these

61
00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.140
proteins will influence a specific person's biological network.

62
00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.180
When you pair intact, correctly folded biologics with continuous digital tracking,

63
00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.900
you eliminate the guesswork of the average patient. The therapy adjusts to the individual's

64
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:11.340
exact reality. We are stepping away from a century of using synthetic chemicals as blunt instruments

65
00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.640
and moving toward a model that leverages the cooperative power of our own biological networks.

66
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.840
Instructional medicine does not force a biochemical reaction.

67
00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.460
By delivering correctly-shaped proteins, it provides the precise reminder the human

68
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.120
body needs to coordinate its own repair. This represents a complete structural

69
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.000
rebuild of how healthcare is discovered, manufactured, and administered.

70
00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:40.880
By replacing synthetic compounds with the endogenous signaling proteins our systems

71
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:48.780
already use, we are delivering a new class of therapeutics. Medicine made by the body for the body.

72
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:52.600
Dramatization: the animations are illustrations, not real footage.
